# Daily engineering routine

Before doing any development work, read AGENTS.md and inspect the GitHub repository.

GitHub Issues are the authoritative source of project work.

Never begin a meaningful feature, bug fix, refactor, or improvement without an associated GitHub
Issue.

When work is completed, create or update a Pull Request, perform a complete engineering
self-review, run all relevant tests and CI checks, correct discovered issues, and merge the PR
when all repository requirements are satisfied.

Update the associated GitHub Issue and project tracking information.

Maintain this workflow across every session. Do not rely on conversation history to remember
project status.

Never falsely report completed work or bypass repository security protections.

A self-review is the author's engineering check. It is not an independent human approval. Do not
describe it as one.
